  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Assistance alimentaire pour les personnes affect&#xE9;es et connectivit&#xE9; a&#xE9;rienne pour les organisations humanitaires en r&#xE9;ponse au passage du cyclone Gamane dans le Nord de Madagascar</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective  for WFP Food assistance for affected individuals and air services for humanitarian organizations in response to the passage of Cyclone Gamane in northern Madagascar.WFP plans to aid 10,697 households with food supplies and cash transfers for one month, addressing immediate food needs amid harvest shortages and preparing for the upcoming farming season. WFP/UNHAS will extend flight hours for its 19-seater aircraft for three months, facilitating bi-weekly air connectivity to affected areas like Maroantsetra, Antalaha, Sambava, Vohemar, and Ambilobe. Special inter-agency mission flights will assess needs in inaccessible areas, expediting response and supply delivery. WFP will target a total of 53,0229 people, including 11,062 women, 6,494 men, 35,466 children, and 999 persons with disabilities</narrative>
  </description>
